# The build context is the repository. Keep out what the image never needs and
# what would bust the layer cache on every commit.
.git
.github
node_modules
dist
*.tgz

# The builder stage does `COPY . .` over the whole context; the runtime stage
# only ever copies the npm pack tarball out of it, so `.env` never reaches the
# final image either way. It does land in a local builder layer and the build
# cache for anyone building from a checkout with a filled `.env`
# (compose.build.yml), which is what this keeps out. `.env.example` carries no
# secret and is documentation, so it is re-included after the exclusion below.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Documentation and fixtures. `example-vault/` is deliberately kept: the
# clean-room golden check runs `gamereg build` over its event log inside the
# image, which is the one test a container can run and a host cannot.
docs
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
SECURITY.md
